 "equipment_type": "Room panel (thermostat display)",
 "applies_to": "iSMA CONTROLLI Control Point room panels, including the VAV version used with the iSMA-B-VAV14-IP controller.",
 "summary": "The Control Point room panel exposes its built-in temperature, humidity and CO2 sensors, a temperature setpoint with offset, fan mode and speed, occupancy mode and status, and its display and keypad settings as BACnet objects. The VAV version adds a commissioning submenu (BO 64-69, MV 5-17, AO 22-37) that mirrors the VAV14-IP controller settings: airflow limits, K-factor, damper and fan test commands. Seven menus of user-defined parameters let the BMS show its own values.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "Control Point Software manual V1.1",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "The manual table mixes objects and object properties. Only Present Value rows are listed; rows for other properties (offset, filter, limits, names, visibility, Device-object properties such as BACNET_DEVICE_ID and BAUD_RATE) are left out.",
  "AV 58 OFFSET_SETPOINT and MV 2 FAN_TYPE are printed with a property number (1503, 1602) instead of Present value; they are listed because the Touch Point manuals show them as Present value objects. DEFAULT_SETPOINT is printed as \"AC57\" and listed as AV 57.",
  "BO 14-24 are all named LCD_ICON_DISPLAY (one per icon, given in the description); BO 25-35 LCD_ICON_FLASHING is a range shown by its first object.",
  "The VAV submenu objects come from a separate page; each one is linked to a VAV14-IP application object (named in the manual). AO 23 is printed twice there and listed once.",
  "User-defined parameter slots (NUMERIC1-8 as AV 0-55, BOOLEAN1-8 as BV 0-55) for the main menu and six submenus are all listed; the manual gives no Present value row for MAIN_MENU_NUMERIC3 and NUMERIC7 (AV 2, AV 6)."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Control Point Software User Manual V1.1 - List of BACnet Objects",
  "doc_number": null,
  "revision_date": "V1.1",
  "url": "https://icdocs.ismacontrolli.com/control-point-software/V1.1/list-of-bacnet-objects"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Read the room temperature (AI 4), humidity (AI 5), CO2 (AI 6) and effective setpoint (AI 3); write the setpoint (AV 56), fan mode (MV 1) and occupancy mode (MV 4) from the BMS. BO 62 switches occupancy between local and BMS mode. With a VAV14-IP the VAV submenu objects are commissioning settings only.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "MV 4",
    "name": "OCCUPANCY_MODE",
    "why": "Occupancy mode, 1 = unoccupied, 2 = occupied"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 56",
    "name": "SETPOINT",
    "why": "Temperature setpoint"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 1",
    "name": "FAN_MODE",
    "why": "Fan mode: 1 off, 2-4 manual speed, 5 auto"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 4",
    "name": "TEMPERATURE_SENSOR",
    "why": "Room temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 3",
    "name": "EFFECTIVE_SETPOINT",
    "why": "Effective setpoint (setpoint plus offset)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 3",
    "name": "CURRENT_OCCUPIED_STATUS",
    "why": "Occupancy status: 0 unocc, 1 occ, 2 standby, 3 forced"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 5",
    "name": "HUMIDITY_SENSOR",
    "why": "Room humidity"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 6",
    "name": "CO2_SENSOR",
    "why": "Room CO2"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "BO 62 OCCUPIED_CONFIG_LOCAL_MODE selects local or BMS occupancy mode.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Device instance and baud rate are Device-object properties (BACNET_DEVICE_ID default 0xFFFFFFFF, BAUD_RATE default 115200).",
   "The VAV submenu (password AO 36, default 1000) is for commissioning the VAV14-IP from the panel."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Most configuration objects are stored in panel memory; avoid cyclic writes.",
   "Sensor objects exist only on panel versions with that sensor (MI 1 SENSORS lists them)."
  ]
 },
